# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need — cmd/hackerfive/dotenv.go
# loads .env from the current working directory automatically, for every
# subcommand (scan/serve/mcp-serve/...), on Windows and macOS/Linux alike.
# A real environment variable you've already exported always wins over
# whatever's in .env — this file only fills in what isn't already set.
#
# Never commit a real .env file — it's already in .gitignore.

# --- Scan credentials (cmd/hackerfive/scan.go, pkg/mcpserver's scan/plan tools) ---
# Owner-account auth token for idor/authbypass/businesslogic detectors.
# HACKERFIVE_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Second, unrelated account's token — idor's cross-account baseline comparison.
# HACKERFIVE_OTHER_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- HackerOne report submission (cmd/hackerfive/report.go) ---
# HACKERONE_API_USERNAME=
# HACKERONE_API_TOKEN=
# HACKERONE_API_BASE_URL=

# --- Phase 6 Step 2: tiered LLM fallback (pkg/llmfallback) ---
# Only used by the MCP server's plan/findings.triage tools, and only when a
# leaf/field the deterministic decision engine couldn't resolve needs an
# LLM's help. Local tier is tried first and costs nothing; OpenRouter is
# used only for drafting a genuinely new template.

# Local model runtime base URL, OpenAI-chat-completions-compatible (Ollama
# and similar). Default if unset: http://localhost:11434
# HACKERFIVE_LOCAL_MODEL_URL=http://localhost:11434

# Which local model to request — must already be pulled/available on that
# runtime. Default if unset: llama3.1 (a placeholder, not a recommendation —
# set this to whatever you actually have, e.g. `ollama list`).
# HACKERFIVE_LOCAL_MODEL_NAME=llama3.1

# OpenRouter API key. Leave unset to disable the frontier tier entirely —
# the local tier still works on its own for the routine leaf/field cases.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter model ID (see https://openrouter.ai/models for the current
# catalog — the default below is a placeholder, not a verified-current ID).
# HACKERFIVE_OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/auto

# Per-1M-token USD prices for the configured OpenRouter model, used to
# compute each call's real cost against the spend ceilings below. Confirm
# the real current price for whatever model you set above.
# HACKERFIVE_OPENROUTER_PRICE_PER_1M_INPUT_USD=3.0
# HACKERFIVE_OPENROUTER_PRICE_PER_1M_OUTPUT_USD=15.0

# Default per-plan-call spend ceiling (USD) — how much one `plan` or
# `findings.triage` call's own LLM-fallback resolution pass may spend before
# remaining misses just escalate to a human instead of burning more budget.
# Overridable per call via the plan tool's own spend_ceiling_usd argument.
# HACKERFIVE_SPEND_CEILING_USD=0.10

# Process-lifetime cumulative spend ceiling (USD), across every plan/
# findings.triage call this server process makes — the guard that actually
# matters if an agent is expected to run many plan calls over a session.
# HACKERFIVE_SPEND_CEILING_TOTAL_USD=2.00
